WEBVTT

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
bokura nara daijoubu

00:00:02.860 --> 00:00:05.930
Because we’re still doing okay,

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:00:05.930 --> 00:00:12.390
we can become even stronger!

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
takaihiroi sora megake

00:00:15.460 --> 00:00:17.900
Aiming for the tall and wide sky,

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
kinou made no boku wo hanatsu

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.450
I let go of what I was up until yesterday.

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
miesuita uso mo, taikutsu na

00:00:21.450 --> 00:00:24.260
Those lies that were easily seen through and my tedious day-by-day life;

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
hibi mo, zenbu hodoite

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.980
I left them both behind.

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
atarashii asa ni me wo hosome

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:29.870
I narrowed my eyes at the new morning

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
kyou mo bokutachi wa ikiteku

00:00:29.870 --> 00:00:33.280
Today we shall also venture out
to live our lives again.

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
sukoshi nami utsu sabishisadatte

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:36.720
Even the slight loneliness that sometimes comes about,

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
taisetsu ni omoeteru

00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:39.460
I consider important.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
itsuka kanjita shinjitsu mo

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:45.070
Even the truth I felt some day…

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
massugu koko kara asu ni mukatteru

00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:51.440
…is urging us to go on into the future.

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
bokutachi ga mezashita sekai

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:56.450
The world that we had all aimed for…

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
donna kakomo kakaeta mama kitto tadoritsuku

00:00:56.450 --> 00:01:03.470
We will arrive at it, no matter what our pasts are.

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.500
fumidashita kewashii michi mo

00:01:03.470 --> 00:01:08.500
We continued forward, even if it is a steep path…

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.900
bokura nara daijoubu,

00:01:08.500 --> 00:01:11.900
…because we’re still doing okay,

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
mada tsuyoku nareru kara

00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:18.280
and we can become even stronger!

00:01:37.220 --> 00:01:39.520
Eh? Sunday, as in tomorrow?

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:42.560
I’m not doing anything in particular…

00:01:42.560 --> 00:01:45.340
We know this really cute cafe!

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.270
They only sell twenty strawberry tarts
daily; and I hear it’s superb!

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:51.400
This is definitely a rarity!

00:01:51.400 --> 00:01:55.720
Hey, Nozomu-chan, didn’t you like eating strawberry desserts best?

00:01:55.720 --> 00:01:58.950
Strawberry ice cream or strawberry shortcakes…

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:02.580
Well yeah… I don’t mind going with you guys, but…

00:02:04.590 --> 00:02:05.410
Really?

00:02:05.410 --> 00:02:06.370
I’m so happy!

00:02:06.370 --> 00:02:08.370
Let’s wait at the cafe then!

00:02:08.370 --> 00:02:10.500
Would 2pm be okay for you?

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:13.250
Maybe 2pm would be a nice time.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:17.080
But if we leave too early it’ll be lunch time and there will be a crowd.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:21.140
Umm… where is this store?

00:02:21.140 --> 00:02:24.970
It’s to the right of the tobacco shop on the street in front of the train station.

00:02:24.970 --> 00:02:27.730
There’s a tobacco shop in front of the train station?

00:02:27.730 --> 00:02:30.400
Sheesh, you’ve forgotten it?

00:02:30.400 --> 00:02:33.060
It’s diagonally across
from the grocery store.

00:02:33.060 --> 00:02:34.270
Grocery?

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:38.570
You’re wrong, Kaoruko! The grocery store became a convenience store, right?

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:41.620
Is that so? Wasn’t that
the hardware shop?

00:02:42.390 --> 00:02:44.330
Sheesh! Onii-chan, hurry!

00:02:44.330 --> 00:02:45.870
Quit hogging the phone!

00:02:45.870 --> 00:02:48.480
Didn’t you say we’d go shopping for groceries together?

00:02:48.870 --> 00:02:51.710
The discount meat will be sold out!

00:02:51.710 --> 00:02:53.920
Sorry! Just wait a bit longer.

00:02:53.920 --> 00:02:56.840
Sorry, I didn’t know
you were about to leave.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:02:59.400
We’ll fax you the time and a map, then.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.760
Onii-chan, hurry!

00:03:00.300 --> 00:03:01.390
I got it!

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:02.910
Hurry up!!!

00:03:03.550 --> 00:03:06.270
I got it, I got it! Quit pulling me!

00:03:11.730 --> 00:03:15.230
There will be widespread rain tomorrow as the rainy season continues.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:17.880
The chance of rain is 100%.

00:03:17.880 --> 00:03:19.820
100%?

00:03:19.820 --> 00:03:23.760
We’ve finally reached Papa’s 12th trial!

00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:27.080
To go shopping in the rain with umbrellas.

00:03:27.080 --> 00:03:29.160
It’s different from regular shopping.

00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.560
We must be extra careful!

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:34.170
We need to hold the umbrella in the right hand while holding the bag in the left hand.

00:03:34.170 --> 00:03:38.570
But what do we do with the umbrellas when we have to get the purse?

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:50.890
I guess I can consider this a date… a first date.

00:03:50.890 --> 00:03:52.650
Is it okay to be that direct?

00:03:53.230 --> 00:03:58.280
No, maybe if the twins are so direct, then it’s just going out with friends and not a date.

00:03:59.110 --> 00:04:01.880
No, maybe it’s good to start off as just friends.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:04.360
Why do you look so happy?

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:05.640
Where are you going tomorrow?

00:04:05.640 --> 00:04:07.940
Um, somewhere.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.290
I want to go!

00:04:09.290 --> 00:04:09.950
Me too!

00:04:09.950 --> 00:04:13.940
What are you talking about? Aren’t you going to Grandma’s house to play?

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.420
I don’t wanna!

00:04:15.420 --> 00:04:16.900
I wanna be with Onii-chan!

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.800
Don’t make unreasonable demands.

00:04:22.010 --> 00:04:25.780
Which reminds me… Miyabi-san, was there a fax for me?

00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:28.700
A fax? I don’t know. I haven’t seen one.

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:31.430
It hasn’t been sent?

00:04:31.430 --> 00:04:34.710
Don’t tell me they forgot?

00:04:37.770 --> 00:04:42.190
Billy, what’s wrong?
You have no appetite?

00:04:42.190 --> 00:04:44.790
If you don’t eat enough,
you won’t grow big.

00:05:01.380 --> 00:05:02.700
So, it’s raining.

00:05:03.380 --> 00:05:07.280
I wanted to eat the strawberry tart at an open terrace.

00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:09.600
That can’t be helped since it’s the rainy season.

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:14.290
Also, they say that freshly baked bread is tastier on humid days, right?

00:05:14.770 --> 00:05:17.210
But aren’t bread and tarts different?

00:05:17.210 --> 00:05:21.670
Don’t worry. Tomorrow’s tarts will definitely be twice as good as normal!

00:05:23.740 --> 00:05:26.950
I’m going off now,
so I’ll leave the rest to you.

00:05:26.950 --> 00:05:29.210
Don’t cheat on us!

00:05:29.820 --> 00:05:31.600
Be careful!

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:36.130
Looks like it wasn’t sent.

00:05:36.540 --> 00:05:38.610
Maybe I should call to ask them.

00:05:42.250 --> 00:05:44.990
Speaking of which…
I don’t know their phone number.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.590
Is there some kind of a memo?

00:05:47.590 --> 00:05:48.690
Ummm…

00:05:49.260 --> 00:05:50.000
Miyabi-san!

00:05:51.390 --> 00:05:53.080
What’s the Ichijous’ phone number?

00:05:56.020 --> 00:05:57.340
I’m too late.

00:06:00.190 --> 00:06:01.730
Be quiet, Billy!

00:06:01.730 --> 00:06:03.590
I don’t have the time
to mess with you now!

00:06:06.440 --> 00:06:09.250
Billy? What’s wrong, Billy?

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:11.580
Not at a time like this!

00:06:12.660 --> 00:06:15.060
Are you sure you’ll be okay, Misses?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:19.060
At least let me drive you to the vicinity of the store.

00:06:19.060 --> 00:06:22.130
Thank you, Kenmochi-san,
but we’ll be okay.

00:06:22.130 --> 00:06:25.400
It doesn’t count as a trial if we don’t use our umbrellas from the front door.

00:06:26.340 --> 00:06:27.900
Misses…

00:06:30.380 --> 00:06:32.180
Let’s go, Yura-chan.

00:06:32.180 --> 00:06:33.600
Yes, Kira-chan.

00:06:41.270 --> 00:06:44.170
The Misses have become stronger.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:02.400
Sign: Chigusa Veterinarian Hospital

00:07:22.310 --> 00:07:23.300
Errr…

00:07:26.170 --> 00:07:31.610
Ui-chan, what do we do?
It’s a guy! Why is he here?

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:33.320
Should we call 110?

00:07:31.610 --> 00:07:35.850
Note: 110 is the Japanese equivalent of 911 in the USA

00:07:33.320 --> 00:07:35.850
Wait! Calm down, Koi-chan!

00:07:35.850 --> 00:07:36.530
But…

00:07:36.530 --> 00:07:39.620
Umm, you’re wrong!
I’m not a suspicious person!

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:40.520
It’s an emergency!

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:51.720
Umm… it’s a young goat.
It suddenly became sick.

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:56.660
Ah, yes… Umm, Mr. Young Goat?
That’s a really rare name.

00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.830
Umm, no. It’s a young goat, a pet.

00:07:59.830 --> 00:08:03.340
Oh, I’m sorry… It’s a goat.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:05.360
Come on in.

00:08:14.360 --> 00:08:16.680
Umm, do you happen to be twins?

00:08:17.620 --> 00:08:20.000
Yes, I’m Chigusa Ui.

00:08:20.000 --> 00:08:21.180
I’m Koi.

00:08:21.870 --> 00:08:23.820
ANOTHER set of twins?

00:08:27.920 --> 00:08:32.470
He didn’t have any appetite yesterday, and he’s been like this since morning.

00:08:33.130 --> 00:08:36.660
Umm, I’m sorry…
Father is out on a house call.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:40.600
The two of us can’t see
to patients very well.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:44.420
I’m sorry! Can you wait until Father gets back?

00:08:44.850 --> 00:08:46.920
Oh. Is that so?

00:08:46.920 --> 00:08:51.120
Umm, it’s not like that…
I think he’ll be back soon.

00:08:51.610 --> 00:08:55.720
Yamada-san’s Sebastian seems to have become sick suddenly!

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.680
Sebastian?

00:08:58.660 --> 00:09:03.420
Sebastian is the name of
Yamada-san’s pet armadillo.

00:09:03.420 --> 00:09:08.060
I’m sorry! It sounds like a butler’s name!

00:09:08.060 --> 00:09:12.570
But Yamada-san’s butler
is called Saito-san.

00:09:15.510 --> 00:09:18.510
What’s this child’s name?

00:09:18.510 --> 00:09:19.800
It’s Billy.

00:09:19.800 --> 00:09:23.780
Billy, hang in there!
Bear with it just a bit longer.

00:09:25.440 --> 00:09:27.150
What is it, Ui-chan?

00:09:27.150 --> 00:09:30.050
I feel something in his throat.

00:09:35.070 --> 00:09:37.200
He seems to have swallowed this.

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.560
Because of this piece of paper…

00:09:43.120 --> 00:09:44.830
Something seems to be written on it.

00:09:44.830 --> 00:09:47.820
“Nozomu-chan, we’ll be waiting for you here at 2!”

00:09:48.420 --> 00:09:50.430
That’s the fax!

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:53.680
Billy ate it.

00:09:56.550 --> 00:09:59.780
Thank goodness, there’s still plenty of time before 2pm!

00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:03.540
Umm, is your name “Nozomi-san”?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:06.040
No, it’s Nozomu.

00:10:06.890 --> 00:10:08.370
“Young Goat Nozomu-san”?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:12.380
Umm, no… I’m not called “Young Goat”.

00:10:17.360 --> 00:10:19.160
What do we do, Kira-chan?

00:10:19.160 --> 00:10:20.990
There’s lightning.

00:10:20.990 --> 00:10:25.080
Buying things during lightning is trial #37.

00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:27.270
We’ll get to do two trials at once!

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:30.510
Oh, what is it?

00:10:31.920 --> 00:10:33.400
Yura-chan, over there.

00:10:33.920 --> 00:10:35.180
It’s a kitten.

00:10:35.630 --> 00:10:37.640
Did it get hit by a car?

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:42.720
What do we do, Kira-chan? There isn’t anything like this in Papa’s trials.

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:45.270
Even though this isn’t a trial,
we still have to save it!

00:10:45.270 --> 00:10:46.920
Yeah. That’s right.

00:10:52.150 --> 00:10:54.900
I’ll pick him up later, then.

00:10:54.900 --> 00:10:57.400
I’ll ask Father to take a look when he returns.

00:10:57.400 --> 00:11:00.030
However, I think he’ll be okay.

00:11:00.030 --> 00:11:01.250
Please take care of him.

00:11:06.810 --> 00:11:08.420
I’m sorry!

00:11:12.630 --> 00:11:14.510
The animals are starting to get restless!

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:17.720
I’m going to go take a look!

00:11:27.100 --> 00:11:29.690
Katherine! Don’t do it!

00:11:35.400 --> 00:11:36.530
What’s going on?

00:11:37.730 --> 00:11:38.870
Is everything okay?

00:11:48.580 --> 00:11:50.460
What do we do?

00:11:50.460 --> 00:11:51.800
Sheesh, that Katherine!

00:12:06.680 --> 00:12:08.520
Maybe we’re a bit early.

00:12:09.310 --> 00:12:12.150
Let’s order the strawberry tart.

00:12:13.850 --> 00:12:15.150
Welcome.

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.130
That should be all of them.

00:12:22.650 --> 00:12:24.070
Yes, it is.

00:12:24.070 --> 00:12:25.780
Thank you very much.

00:12:25.780 --> 00:12:29.100
You really know how to deal with animals.

00:12:29.580 --> 00:12:31.440
Oh, it’s nothing much.

00:12:32.410 --> 00:12:34.830
Animals can read people.

00:12:34.830 --> 00:12:37.440
They don’t listen to people they dislike.

00:12:38.320 --> 00:12:41.200
You must be kindhearted!

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:44.950
Oh no, I don’t think I’m like that…

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:50.960
This child would never take to strangers, yet she looks so happy.

00:12:54.940 --> 00:12:57.980
We’ve already been taking care of her for a week…

00:12:57.980 --> 00:13:00.160
But she still doesn’t react favorably to us.

00:13:01.230 --> 00:13:02.940
Maybe…

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:05.240
we don’t have kind hearts?

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:06.280
How could that be?

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:09.020
Umm… please tell us how to think,
Young Goat-san.

00:13:09.020 --> 00:13:13.130
Ah, I have an appointment.

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.370
Yes?

00:13:16.370 --> 00:13:17.830
Excuse me?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:18.930
Come on in.

00:13:19.880 --> 00:13:23.780
This kitten was hit by a car!

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:27.310
Nozomu-kun!

00:13:36.020 --> 00:13:37.920
That’s one of the 20 limited ones!

00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:42.640
It looks so good!

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:45.830
I think Nozomu-chan will be happy with that!

00:13:53.480 --> 00:13:55.230
Apparently the hind leg is broken.

00:13:56.040 --> 00:14:00.230
It’s best to operate on it, but we…

00:14:00.670 --> 00:14:04.590
We just got a call;
Father is on his way back.

00:14:04.590 --> 00:14:07.220
So he’ll be back soon.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:10.160
Actually, it seems he went
to another house.

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:11.930
Which house?

00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:12.980
I don’t know.

00:14:13.680 --> 00:14:15.560
Please save this child.

00:14:15.560 --> 00:14:16.420
Please!

00:14:18.850 --> 00:14:21.800
Ah, I think we should do some kind of emergency treatment.

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.400
Emergency treatment?

00:14:24.400 --> 00:14:28.360
I think it’s best to use the painkiller and support it with a splint.

00:14:28.360 --> 00:14:31.660
But the medicines are in a mess.

00:14:31.660 --> 00:14:36.580
And also, we’ve never done an emergency treatment before.

00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:40.790
Let’s do it, Koi-chan! We’re already high-school students.

00:14:40.790 --> 00:14:42.960
It we can’t do something like this…

00:14:42.960 --> 00:14:47.380
You’re right. We’ve watched Father apply dressings all the time.

00:14:47.380 --> 00:14:50.090
We need to find the painkiller first.

00:14:50.090 --> 00:14:51.970
I’ll go ahead and help.

00:14:51.970 --> 00:14:52.950
I’ll help you find it!

00:14:56.220 --> 00:14:57.690
Power outage?

00:15:16.950 --> 00:15:18.660
Umm, is this okay?

00:15:18.660 --> 00:15:19.540
Eh?

00:15:19.540 --> 00:15:21.290
Weren’t you going to meet someone?

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:24.520
Yeah, but I can’t just ignore this.

00:15:25.980 --> 00:15:27.530
You’re so kind.

00:15:27.920 --> 00:15:30.030
It’s nothing.

00:15:32.050 --> 00:15:33.560
I’m sorry!

00:15:39.180 --> 00:15:40.850
There’s no one there.

00:15:40.850 --> 00:15:43.030
Maybe he’s on his way right now?

00:15:44.560 --> 00:15:46.000
Let’s wait a bit longer.

00:16:10.170 --> 00:16:11.120
What is it?

00:16:15.430 --> 00:16:16.400
What’s wrong?

00:16:17.430 --> 00:16:18.690
John’s here!

00:16:19.240 --> 00:16:20.190
John?

00:16:21.560 --> 00:16:23.940
Something just brushed at my leg!

00:16:23.940 --> 00:16:25.780
It’s underneath that table!

00:16:26.860 --> 00:16:30.190
When Katherine escaped, it must have escaped along with it.

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.110
If we don’t grab it quickly…

00:16:32.110 --> 00:16:34.580
Everyone, don’t move! I’ll grab it!

00:16:36.800 --> 00:16:38.440
John! John, come on out!

00:16:39.580 --> 00:16:41.660
It’s very dangerous
if you get too close!

00:16:41.660 --> 00:16:44.630
Don’t worry. Leave me
to handle the animal.

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.050
Hmm? It feels really hard.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:53.070
The power outage is over.

00:16:59.730 --> 00:17:01.120
John is an ALLIGATOR?!?!?

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:04.190
He’s a Mississippi alligator.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:06.630
He’s hospitalized for cavity treatment.

00:17:11.690 --> 00:17:12.840
What should we do?

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.120
It’s really small.

00:17:18.120 --> 00:17:20.410
Even though it’s small,
an alligator is still an alligator!

00:17:20.410 --> 00:17:22.140
If we get bitten,
we’ll be in deep trouble!

00:17:27.210 --> 00:17:28.260
Billy!

00:17:59.450 --> 00:18:00.680
It should be okay.

00:18:01.240 --> 00:18:03.540
The analgesic seem to be working.

00:18:03.540 --> 00:18:05.290
Thank you very much.

00:18:05.290 --> 00:18:07.380
Hey, I’m back!

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:12.700
There seemed to be a power outage.
Is everything okay?

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:14.470
Father!

00:18:18.020 --> 00:18:20.700
The emergency treatment was well done. Did you guys do it?

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.120
Everyone helped out.

00:18:26.230 --> 00:18:29.000
Um, my name’s Futami Nozomu.

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:36.580
I see! I thought you girls were shy!

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:46.310
I’ll be going now.
I’ll pick up Billy later.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:48.290
Sorry for making you late.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.460
Thank you very much.

00:18:50.460 --> 00:18:52.630
We owe you another favor.

00:18:52.630 --> 00:18:54.780
If you’re in a hurry, we can have Kenmochi-san drive you there.

00:18:56.090 --> 00:18:58.300
I’ll be okay. It’ll be faster if I run there.

00:18:58.300 --> 00:18:59.310
Bye!

00:19:06.930 --> 00:19:08.820
Let’s go home for today.

00:19:09.770 --> 00:19:12.780
Nozomu-chan must have had a reason.

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:35.300
There’s no way they’d still be here.

00:19:44.470 --> 00:19:47.390
I’m sure they’re pretty angry at me.

00:19:47.390 --> 00:19:49.610
But I have to apologize today.

00:19:50.100 --> 00:19:51.490
Okay, let’s muster some courage!

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:55.860
Yes?

00:19:55.860 --> 00:19:58.280
Er, it’s me, Futami.

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:02.220
They’re angry, as I thought.

00:20:09.750 --> 00:20:11.960
Umm… I’m sorry about today.

00:20:11.960 --> 00:20:12.710
Umm…

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.460
We waited for you for TWO HOURS!

00:20:14.460 --> 00:20:16.480
Yeah! It’s cruel that you broke a promise!

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:19.140
I’m sorry! I’m REALLY sorry!

00:20:25.470 --> 00:20:27.440
But we’ll forgive you.

00:20:28.310 --> 00:20:30.790
Since it was all for saving a kitten, right?

00:20:31.500 --> 00:20:34.040
Eh? How did you know?

00:20:35.440 --> 00:20:38.190
Nozomu-chan is definitely kind.

00:20:38.190 --> 00:20:41.340
Yeah! In that respect,
he hasn’t changed from before!

00:20:43.570 --> 00:20:46.600
Let’s go eat a strawberry tart next week, okay?

00:20:50.410 --> 00:20:51.420
Okay!

00:20:53.580 --> 00:20:55.080
So, we’ll see you tomorrow…

00:20:55.080 --> 00:20:56.210
in school!

00:20:56.210 --> 00:20:57.860
See you tomorrow!

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.230
Everything turned out okay, Koi-chan.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:21.740
Yes, it did, Ui-chan.

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:24.040
It looks like they made up.

00:21:27.410 --> 00:21:30.820
But I envy them.

00:21:30.820 --> 00:21:31.340
Yeah.

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:58.050
dokomademo tsuzuku sora

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:58.050
Oh, the sky that continues no matter where you go…

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:04.050
daisuki na kono machi de

00:21:58.050 --> 00:22:04.050
In this town that I love…

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.060
takusan no omoide to, hora,

00:22:04.050 --> 00:22:10.060
With all our memories, now look!

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:16.060
onaji dake hohoende

00:22:10.060 --> 00:22:16.060
We are smiling the same way

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:26.700
itsudemo kimi no tonari ni iyoutoshiteru no wa

00:22:16.060 --> 00:22:26.700
To always be trying to be besides you…

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
mukashi kara no kuse datte omotteru kedo

00:22:26.700 --> 00:22:39.020
…is, I believe, a bad habit I’ve had for a long time

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
“mata ashita” tte te wo furu toki ni wa

00:22:39.020 --> 00:22:45.140
When we wave our hands saying “see you tomorrow,”

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
sukoshi dake samishii kigasuru yo

00:22:45.140 --> 00:22:50.930
I realize that I’m feeling a little lonely at that moment

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
tooku naru kimi no senaka mitsumete

00:22:50.930 --> 00:22:57.230
Staring at your back that is getting further away,

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
nandaka, fushigi na kimochi

00:22:57.230 --> 00:23:03.190
For some reason, a mysterious feeling…

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
kono mune ni hirogatte yuku

00:23:03.190 --> 00:23:09.090
…is spreading through this heart of mine

00:23:10.970 --> 00:23:14.080
Umm… I’m Chigusa Ui.

00:23:14.080 --> 00:23:15.180
I’m Koi.

00:23:15.180 --> 00:23:17.560
Billy tore up…

00:23:17.560 --> 00:23:19.120
Nozomu-san’s notebook!

00:23:19.730 --> 00:23:21.000
Next time:
